{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"state graph","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-four-rules","text":"The four rules","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"gesture + ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"@GestureState","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origami.drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Drag","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"text":" body. Origami ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"text":" means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"text":" modifier — that’s a different concept).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","text":"Pure value patch → computed property","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","level":3,"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","level":3,"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3,"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2,"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","generated":true,"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check."}],"title":"Beats","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"title":"Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"title":"Interaction","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"abstract":[{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Drag","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" patch (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Drag","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"}}}